  <section class="section"><div class="container detail-grid"><aside class="detail-aside"><span class="eyebrow">From brief to approval</span><h3 style="margin-top:16px">Keep scope, budget and decisions connected.</h3><p>Independent coordination helps clients see the full picture before important commitments are made.</p><a class="btn" href="/#contact">Discuss your project <span>↗</span></a></aside><div class="detail-copy"><p class="lead">Whether you are planning a new residence, a major renovation or an upgrade to an existing property, early coordination can save time and reduce uncertainty.</p><h2>What we coordinate</h2><ul><li><strong>Feasibility and brief:</strong> clarify priorities, scope, constraints and decision criteria.</li><li><strong>Design coordination:</strong> support communication between architects, engineers, surveyors and other appointed specialists.</li><li><strong>Cost planning:</strong> develop preliminary estimates, compare options and identify cost drivers.</li><li><strong>Permits and approvals:</strong> coordinate the building-permit process and the professionals responsible for preparing and signing statutory documents.</li><li><strong>Procurement support:</strong> organise tender information, compare offers and clarify scope differences.</li><li><strong>Programme and reporting:</strong> track key decisions, milestones, risks and next steps.</li></ul><h2>Independent, client-focused coordination</h2><p>Our role is to make complex projects easier to understand and manage. We help clients compare options transparently and coordinate the appointed professionals; regulated design work, certifications and formal submissions remain with appropriately qualified and authorised practitioners.</p><div class="callout"><strong>Designed around your project</strong><p style="margin:8px 0 0">Support can begin at the property-search stage, during concept design, before a permit application or after a project is already underway.</p></div></div></div></section>
